# 🚀 BabySoC – Implementation

> 🧑‍💻 A hands-on exploration of the RTL-to-GDSII journey using the **VSDIAT BabySoC**, covering RTL simulation, synthesis, SKY130 technology mapping, and gate-level verification.

---

## 📌 Project Introduction

This project focuses on taking a small **RISC-V based System-on-Chip (SoC)** from its RTL representation toward an ASIC-ready implementation.

The work demonstrates the transition from **behavioral hardware description → synthesized logic → technology-mapped gates → post-synthesis verification**.

The primary tools used in this stage of the flow are **Icarus Verilog, GTKWave, Yosys, ABC, and the SKY130 standard-cell library**.

---

# 🏗️ BabySoC Structure

The BabySoC integrates three important functional blocks:

| Block           | Purpose                                                             |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 🧠 **RVMyth**   | RISC-V based processor and digital logic                            |
| 🔄 **AVSDPLL**  | Generates the clock used by the processor                           |
| 🎚️ **AVSDDAC** | Converts the processor's digital output into an analog-style output |

The complete design is controlled through the top-level module:

```text
vsdbabysoc
```

---

## 🔗 Functional Data Path

```text
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │    AVSDPLL      │
                    │      PLL        │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │
                           CLK
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │     RVMyth      │
                    │   RISC-V Core   │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │
                      RV_TO_DAC[9:0]
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │     AVSDDAC     │
                    │       DAC       │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                            OUT
```

The processor generates the 10-bit `RV_TO_DAC[9:0]` data bus, which is then connected to the DAC.

The PLL output provides the clock required by the digital processor.

---

# 🌳 Module Hierarchy

The main hierarchy of the SoC can be represented as:

```text
vsdbabysoc
│
├── avsddpll
│
├── rvmyth
│
└── avsddac
```

At the center of the design is `rvmyth`, which performs the digital processing and produces the output data for the DAC.

---

